.TH CTPROBE 1 "2026-08-26" "ctprobe 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ctprobe \- Certificate Transparency subdomain enumeration and HTTP/S reconnaissance
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ctprobe
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.I domain
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ctprobe
queries Certificate Transparency logs for an apex domain, enumerates the unique
certificate-derived subdomains, and optionally probes and classifies their
HTTP/S reachability. It is intended for authorized security assessments and
OSINT reconnaissance.
.PP
The discovery target is normalized using a public-suffix-aware apex derivation,
so inputs such as a full URL or a deep subdomain are reduced to the correct
registrable domain before querying.
.PP
.B ctprobe
is not an anonymity or evasion tool. The
.B \-\-stealth
option only lowers request rate and concurrency; it does not make traffic
anonymous or undetectable. Use this tool only against systems you are
authorized to test.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS Target
.TP
.I domain
Target domain, e.g.\& \fBexample.com\fR. A full URL is accepted and normalized.
.SS Live testing
.TP
.B \-\-live
Perform HTTP live testing on discovered subdomains.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-live
Skip live testing. Conflicts with \fB\-\-match\-code\fR/\fB\-\-filter\-code\fR.
.TP
.BR \-mc ", " \-\-match\-code " " \fISTATUS\fR
Match HTTP status codes, or \fBall\fR. Accepts codes, comma lists, and ranges
(e.g.\& \fB200,301,500\-599\fR). Supplying this option enables live testing.
.TP
.BR \-fc ", " \-\-filter\-code " " \fISTATUS\fR
Exclude status codes from matching responses. Filter takes precedence over
match. Supplying this option enables live testing.
.SS HTTP
.TP
.B \-\-http\-version \fR{auto,1.1,2,3}
Protocol selection. \fBauto\fR tries HTTP/3, HTTP/2, then HTTP/1.1 among the
protocols actually available in the runtime. Default: \fBauto\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-force
Do not fall back to another HTTP version. Requires an explicit
\fB\-\-http\-version\fR. A silently downgraded protocol is rejected.
.TP
.B \-\-bypass\-ssl\fR, \fB\-\-bypass\-tls
Disable TLS certificate verification for the scanner transport only. Insecure;
authorized testing only.
.TP
.B \-\-header \fINAME:VALUE\fR
Add a custom header (repeatable). Control characters are rejected. An explicit
\fBUser-Agent\fR header takes precedence over \fB\-\-user\-agent\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-user\-agent \fISTRING\fR
User-Agent value (default: \fBMozilla/5.0\fR).
.TP
.B \-\-timeout \fISECONDS\fR
Per-request timeout (default: 10.0).
.SS Proxy and Tor
.TP
.B \-\-proxy \fIURL\fR
Route through an HTTP/HTTPS or SOCKS4/4a/5/5h proxy. SOCKS requires PySocks
(python3-socks). Routing is fail-closed: if the proxy cannot be used, the scan
does not run directly.
.TP
.B \-\-tor \fR[\fIURL\fR]
Route through Tor (default endpoint \fBsocks5h://127.0.0.1:9050\fR). Tor is only
reported when confirmed (IsTor=true); a non-Tor SOCKS proxy is rejected. Cannot
be combined with \fB\-\-proxy\fR.
.SS Concurrency and stealth
.TP
.B \-\-workers \fIN\fR
Effective concurrency (default: 30).
.TP
.B \-\-stealth
Conservative low-rate mode: reduced concurrency and randomized delays. Not an
anonymity feature.
.TP
.B \-\-stealth\-min\-delay \fISECONDS\fR, \fB\-\-stealth\-max\-delay \fISECONDS\fR
Randomized delay bounds for stealth mode (defaults: 1.0 and 3.0).
.SS Analysis and output
.TP
.B \-\-threat
Run heuristic threat indicators (TLD, keywords, structure). Heuristic only, not
a maliciousness verdict.
.TP
.B \-\-output \fR{txt,json,xls,xlsx}
Output format (default: txt). Terminal colors never enter output files.
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-filename " " \fINAME\fR
Custom output base name.
.TP
.B \-\-output\-dir \fIDIR\fR
Output directory (default: Outputs).
.SS Logging
.TP
.BR \-\-verbose ", " \-\-debug ", " \-\-quiet
Verbosity controls.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-color
Disable colored output. Also honored via the \fBNO_COLOR\fR environment
variable.
.SH OUTPUT
Without live testing, one file \fINAME\fR.output.\fIext\fR is written. With live
testing, \fINAME\fR.ALL-output.\fIext\fR (every discovered subdomain) and
\fINAME\fR.LIVE-output.\fIext\fR (matched subdomains only) are written; LIVE is
always a subset of ALL.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Successful execution.
.TP
.B 1
General runtime or discovery failure.
.TP
.B 2
Invalid configuration, or proxy/Tor/forced-protocol verification failure.
.TP
.B 130
Interrupted (SIGINT / Ctrl+C).
.PP
Note: finer-grained per-subsystem exit codes are not currently distinguished.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
When set to a non-empty value, disables colored output.
.TP
.B FORCE_COLOR
When set to \fB1\fR, forces colored output.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Enumerate subdomains and prompt for live testing:
.B ctprobe example.com
.TP
Enumerate subdomains and match only HTTP 200 (auto-enables live testing):
.B ctprobe example.com \-mc 200
.TP
Match all responses except 404, JSON output:
.B ctprobe example.com \-mc all \-fc 404 \-\-output json
.TP
Route through Tor with conservative rate:
.B ctprobe example.com \-\-tor \-\-stealth
.SH LIMITATIONS
HTTP/2 requires python3-httpx with the h2 backend; HTTP/3 requires a curl binary
built with HTTP/3 support. SOCKS/Tor routing requires python3-socks. Missing
optional dependencies disable only their specific feature.
